# Captured fallback screenshots are build artifacts — keep the dir, not the files
static/fallback/*.png
!static/fallback/.gitkeep
# Capture working directories. cap.py writes the raw dashboard capture, a full
# page-text dump and a gate report per target here. The audited images that
# actually ship live in static/img/systems/; these are intermediates and have
# no place in a public repo.
scripts/shots/
scripts/blocked/
s3-media-backups/
scripts/summary.json

# The capture harness stays OUT of this repo. It is published to GitHub, and
# cap.py / capture_scrub.js contain the live dashboard hostname, an internal
# repo path, the banned-name list and 33 rename rules -- i.e. the complete
# euphemism -> real-name key. Publishing it would undo the whole point of not
# naming the employer on the site. Keep it local; back it up somewhere private.
scripts/cap.py
scripts/capture_scrub.js
scripts/sim_defs.py
scripts/build_platform_map.py
audit-progress-*.md
scripts/banned_terms.local
